{"kind": "finding", "id": "FN-B-run-phone-components-2-b-01", "date": "2026-11-25", "lens": "gap-8", "surface": "phone", "area": "phone/components-2", "refs": ["F-phone-1412", "FN-L4-phone-components-2-01"], "severity": "S4", "title": "With 'Include photos in my backup' on, a failed photo copy shows no message", "what": "Each time the photo backup page opens, it copies the newest progress photos into the folder Android backs up. If that copy (or reading the switch) fails, the error is swallowed: the 'Checking your photos' line simply disappears and the switch stays as it was. The member believes the photos are in the backup when they may not be. The page is currently reachable only by a direct link, so few members see it.", "expected": "When the photo copy fails, the page says the photos could not be added to the backup this time and offers to try again, and the failure is noted for the team.", "evidence": ["apps/mobile/src/components/settings/PhotoBackupCard.tsx:31-46", "apps/mobile/src/components/settings/PhotoBackupCard.tsx:49-53"], "proof": "code-read", "root_cause_key": "photo-backup-sync-failure-swallowed", "who": "members", "how_often": "rarely", "fix_line": "Show a short 'could not add your photos this time' line with Try again when the copy fails", "fix_size": "small", "needs_him": false, "verified": "pending", "status": "open"}
